{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "label": "CircuitBreaker", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Wraps any promise-returning factory and short-circuits when failure is sustained; it does not care what the call is, so an actor ask wraps the same way as an HTTP fetch.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_three_state_machine", "label": "Closed, open, half-open", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Success resets the counter, consecutive failures reaching maxFailures open the breaker, and the first call after the reset timeout probes: success closes, failure re-opens with a fresh probe time.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_isfailure", "label": "isFailure predicate", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Lets an error reject to the caller without incrementing the counter - for 404s and validation failures that are not really service failures.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_calltimeoutms", "label": "callTimeoutMs", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The longest an individual call should take; set it below the upstream normal latency and you declare everything a timeout. Omit it entirely to disable the per-call timeout.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_lazy_probe", "label": "The probe is lazy, not scheduled", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "There is no wake-up timer; the breaker checks the clock on the next call, so nothing happens until traffic arrives.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_half_open_does_not_queue", "label": "Half-open does not serialize", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Concurrent calls during half-open all go through and the state transition follows whichever completes first; the breaker is not a semaphore, so serialize above it if only one probe matters.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_one_per_dependency", "label": "One breaker per logical dependency", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A single breaker fronting two unrelated dependencies trips on either failure and locks out both; also, a breaker held as an actor field resets on every restart, so hoist it to an extension if the state must survive.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_retry_inside_breaker", "label": "Retry inside the breaker call", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Retry is per-call resilience and the breaker is cross-call coordination; putting the retry outside means retrying through CircuitBreakerOpenErrors, which is pointless.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_three_state_machine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_isfailure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_calltimeoutms", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_lazy_probe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_half_open_does_not_queue", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_patterns_circuit_breaker_one_per_dependency", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/patterns/circuit-breaker.mdx", "sourc